worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_dispatch.js"
  ceiling 146
  rationale "Synchronous browser-handler capability bindings extracted from the universal dispatcher; this table disappears when the Rust-to-WASM dispatcher replaces the JavaScript mirror. Ceiling moved 80 to 111 for issue #1175 R3 (2026-10-07): claimRouteAdmits, the browser twin of rust/src/capability_routing/claims.rs, reads the claim rows of data/seed/capability-routing.lino and offers a handler the prompt only when one of its admits_on evidence kinds holds. Ceiling moved 111 to 117 for issue #1175 R3 (2026-10-07, second pass): six more claim rows (page_query_text, javascript_execution, incompatible_units, http_fetch, url_navigate, calendar_create_event) each need one evidence predicate bound to the worker function the handler already gates on, and claimRouteAdmits passes the handler's own normalized reading. Ceiling moved 117 to 138 for issue #1175 R3 refusal lane (2026-10-07): a claim row may name a refusal_event, kept only when the handler recorded it (test_generation, code_refactoring, format_conversion rows), and issue #1177 R9 binds the CSV-to-JSON evidence predicate. Ceiling moved 138 to 146 for issue #1175 R3 classes b, c and e (2026-10-08): claimRouteAdmission passes the dialogue history to the evidence kinds, claimRouteRun runs any handler (synchronous or the inline asynchronous lookups of formal_ai_worker_20.js) through its row with the refusal lane, and CLAIM_EVIDENCE spreads the class kinds of formal_ai_worker_claim_evidence.js."
